#
# The screens a Quadra run ends on, one a line:
#   <machine> <disk, or none> <screen hash> <what it shows>
# The hash is sim/mame/quadra.lua's: an FNV-1a of the screen's pixels with the
# menu bar's clock masked (MAME's RTC starts from the host's time). MAME is
# deterministic otherwise: the same build, ROMs, disk and options give the
# same screens. make quadra-m68040 runs MAME's own CPU until one of its
# machine's screens holds; make quadra and quadra-lc run the core's machines
# until the reference machine's does. The PNGs are never committed (Apple
# firmware and software output). With the ADB modem's firmware the user
# supplied (342s0440-b.bin) and mac761.chd (System 7.6.1), from M14:
macqd650 mac761 2078a196 the Finder, System 7.6.1: the disk's window, the menu bar, the Control Strip
macct650 mac761 2078a196 the Finder, System 7.6.1: the disk's window, the menu bar, the Control Strip
